<!--
  Source:   https://swissdevjobs.ch/rss
  Captured: 2026-08-23 (feed lastBuildDate 2026-08-22)
  Kept verbatim: the rss/channel envelope with its namespaces, every <item> child tag the parser
    reads (title, link, guid, pubDate, description), and both href forms including the
    ?utm_source=our_rss_feed query the live feed appends to link *and* guid.
  Cut: 172 of 176 items; the <image>, <category> and <atom:link> channel blocks; the per-item
    <enclosure>; and each description's body down to its first two elements (the live median is
    ~2.9 KB of <ul>/<br> markup). <content:encoded> is cut entirely — it is byte-identical to
    <description> in all 176 live items, which is why the adapter reads only one of them.
  Encodes, adversarially:
    - item 1: the normal shape — role, " @ ", company, and a trailing [CHF x - y] bracket that must
      be stripped off the title and must not become part of the company.
    - item 2: a role containing its own " @ ", so the split has to be on the *last* one.
    - item 3: no " @ " at all → company null, title untouched, and an unparseable <pubDate> → null.
    - item 4: a duplicate of item 1's link, which must be dropped rather than overwrite it, and an
      empty <description> → null.
-->
